     A* Literals, hexadecimal constants, continuation, and command keys.
     A* Member: DSPCONST   Compilable: yes
     A* Source: IBM i 7.5 DDS for display files. Retrieved: 2026-07-25
     A*
00010A          R SCREEN1
     A* A constant is a quoted literal with a position but no name.
00020A                                  1 25'CUSTOMER MAINTENANCE'
00030A                                  3  2'Customer''s name:'
     A*
     A* + continues a literal, discarding leading blanks.
00040A                                  5  2'A heading that runs +
00050A                                      across two source lines'
     A* - continues a literal, preserving leading blanks.
00060A                                  6  2'PRESERVED    -
00070A                                           SPACING'
     A*
     A* Hexadecimal constants.
00080A                                  7  2X'40404040'
00090A            HEXDFT         2A  B  8  2DFT(X'C1C2')
     A*
     A* Command attention and command function keys.
00100A                                      CA01(01 'Help')
00110A                                      CA03(03 'Exit')
00120A                                      CF04(04 'Prompt')
00130A                                      CF12(12 'Cancel')
00140A                                      CA24(24 'More keys')
     A*
     A* A field named CA01 must NOT be mistaken for a command key,
     A* and a record named SFL must not be mistaken for a keyword.
00150A            CA01           5A  B 10  2
00160A          R SFL
00170A            CMP            5A  B 11  2
